---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ListItem from "../../../components/ui/ListItem.astro";

import EngDesignFabIcon from "../../../assets/courses/eng-design-fab/img/eng-design-fab-icon.svg";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="py-5 mb-3 bg-sn-darker bottom-shadow">
    <div class="p-5">
      <a href="/#course-content" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light"
        ><i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back</a
      >
    </div>
    <div class="container pb-5">
      <div class="text-center">
        <h1>Engineering: Design and Fabrication</h1>
        <EngDesignFabIcon width={128} height={128} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <h3>About This Course</h3>

        <p>
          <b class="text-sn-theme">Build physical things, then prove they
          work.</b> Unit 1 is the design cycle, precision, tolerance and
          measurement, aimed at a racquet ball launcher you test with real
          data. Unit 2 moves to digital manufacturing &mdash; CAD to CAM to the
          CNC &mdash; and an arcade cabinet.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-5">How You'll Work</h3>

        <p>
          You'll work in <b>teams</b> for almost everything in this course
          &mdash; every build, every lab, and both major projects. Assume team
          work unless a session says otherwise.
        </p>

        <p>
          Three things are always <b>yours alone</b>, even on a team session:
          the <b>reflection</b> at the end of every session, every{" "}
          <b>quiz and practical</b>, and your <b>safety certifications</b>.
          Those are how you're graded as an individual, so a teammate can't do
          them for you and you can't do them for a teammate.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-5">How You're Graded</h3>

        <p>
          Each unit is worth <b class="text-sn-theme">500 points</b>, and both
          units are weighted the same way.
        </p>

        <div class="table-responsive">
          <table class="table table-sm align-middle">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Where the points come from</th>
                <th class="text-end">Unit 1</th>
                <th class="text-end">Unit 2</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><b>Project milestones</b></td>
                <td class="text-end">250</td>
                <td class="text-end">230</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Daily session work</td>
                <td class="text-end">140</td>
                <td class="text-end">100</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Practice build</td>
                <td class="text-end">&mdash;</td>
                <td class="text-end">60</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Quizzes</td>
                <td class="text-end">50</td>
                <td class="text-end">50</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Practicals</td>
                <td class="text-end">25</td>
                <td class="text-end">25</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Safety certifications</td>
                <td class="text-end">20</td>
                <td class="text-end">20</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Project journal</td>
                <td class="text-end">15</td>
                <td class="text-end">15</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><b>Total</b></td>
                <td class="text-end"><b>500</b></td>
                <td class="text-end"><b>500</b></td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p>
          <b class="text-sn-theme">The project is about half your grade, but it
          is not the half you can lose quietly.</b> Milestones are handed in on
          known dates, so you can see them coming. Daily session work is spread
          across twenty-odd sessions at ten points each &mdash; no single one
          matters much, and missing a run of them is the most common way this
          grade slips.
        </p>

        <p>
          Of those 500 points,{" "}
          <b class="text-sn-theme">137 are earned by you alone</b> &mdash; about
          27% &mdash; and it is the same in both units. That is every
          reflection, every quiz and practical, and both safety certifications.
          A strong team cannot carry you through that share, and you cannot
          carry a teammate through theirs.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-5">Course Content</h3>

        <h4 class="mt-2">Unit 1: Design &amp; Empirical Testing</h4>
        <div class="accordion mb-5" id="unit1Accordion">
          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
              <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                type="button"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#u1g1"
                aria-expanded="false"
                aria-controls="u1g1"
              >
                Part 1: The Design Cycle
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div
              id="u1g1"
              class="accordion-collapse collapse"
              data-bs-parent="#unit1Accordion"
            >
              <div class="accordion-body">
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-1">Session 1: Intro to the Design Cycle</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-2">Session 2: Problem Framing &amp; Notebook Setup</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-3">Session 3: Design &amp; Ideation</a></ListItem>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
              <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                type="button"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#u1g2"
                aria-expanded="false"
                aria-controls="u1g2"
              >
                Part 2: Safety &amp; Precision
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div
              id="u1g2"
              class="accordion-collapse collapse"
              data-bs-parent="#unit1Accordion"
            >
              <div class="accordion-body">
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-4">Session 4: Makerspace Safety I</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-5">Session 5: Makerspace Safety II</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-6">Session 6: Caliper Use &amp; Precision</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-7">Session 7: Unit Conversion I</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-8">Session 8: Unit Conversion II &mdash; Applied Dimensional Analysis</a></ListItem>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
              <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                type="button"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#u1g3"
                aria-expanded="false"
                aria-controls="u1g3"
              >
                Part 3: Tolerance
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div
              id="u1g3"
              class="accordion-collapse collapse"
              data-bs-parent="#unit1Accordion"
            >
              <div class="accordion-body">
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-9">Session 9: Tolerance Concepts</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-10">Session 10: The Mismatch Activity + Debrief</a></ListItem>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
              <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                type="button"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#u1g4"
                aria-expanded="false"
                aria-controls="u1g4"
              >
                Part 4: Measurement &amp; Data
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div
              id="u1g4"
              class="accordion-collapse collapse"
              data-bs-parent="#unit1Accordion"
            >
              <div class="accordion-body">
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-11">Session 11: Measurement &amp; Data Collection Lab</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-12">Session 12: Functions &amp; Data Quality in Sheets</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-13">Session 13: Charting &amp; Trendlines</a></ListItem>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
              <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                type="button"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#u1g5"
                aria-expanded="false"
                aria-controls="u1g5"
              >
                Racquet Ball Launcher Project
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div
              id="u1g5"
              class="accordion-collapse collapse"
              data-bs-parent="#unit1Accordion"
            >
              <div class="accordion-body">
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-14-15">Sessions 14&ndash;15: Research &amp; Design</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-16-19">Sessions 16&ndash;19: Build (Iteration 1)</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-20-22">Sessions 20&ndash;22: Test &amp; Calibrate</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-23-24">Sessions 23&ndash;24: Iterate &amp; Re-calibrate</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-25">Session 25: Field Test Day</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-1/session-26">Session 26: Reflect &amp; Defend</a></ListItem>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h4 class="mt-2">Unit 2: Digital Manufacturing</h4>
        <div class="accordion mb-5" id="unit2Accordion">
          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
              <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                type="button"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#u2g1"
                aria-expanded="false"
                aria-controls="u2g1"
              >
                Manufacturing Foundations
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div
              id="u2g1"
              class="accordion-collapse collapse"
              data-bs-parent="#unit2Accordion"
            >
              <div class="accordion-body">
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-1">Session 1: Welcome to Digital Manufacturing</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-2">Session 2: Materials for Subtractive Manufacturing</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-3">Session 3: Additive Manufacturing</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-4">Session 4: CNC Safety Certification</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-5">Session 5: CAD Leveling-Up I &mdash; Assemblies</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-6">Session 6: CAD Leveling-Up II &mdash; A Full Practice Assembly</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-7">Session 7: Toolpath Types &amp; Profile Offset</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-8">Session 8: Pockets, Step-Over &amp; Step-Down</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-9">Session 9: Apply CAM to a Practice Piece</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-10">Session 10: Post-Processing &amp; Troubleshooting</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-11">Session 11: Design Your Practice Build</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-12">Session 12: Program Your Practice Build's CAM</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-13">Session 13: Cut &amp; Evaluate Your Practice Build</a></ListItem>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
              <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                type="button"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#u2g2"
                aria-expanded="false"
                aria-controls="u2g2"
              >
                Arcade Cabinet Project
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div
              id="u2g2"
              class="accordion-collapse collapse"
              data-bs-parent="#unit2Accordion"
            >
              <div class="accordion-body">
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-14-15">Sessions 14&ndash;15: Receive &amp; Translate the Brief</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-16-18">Sessions 16&ndash;18: Concept, Material &amp; CAD</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-19-20">Sessions 19&ndash;20: CAM Programming</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-21-24">Sessions 21&ndash;24: Fabrication &amp; Build</a></ListItem>
                <ListItem><a href="./unit-2/session-25-26">Sessions 25&ndash;26: Present Back &amp; Reflect</a></ListItem>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
